    <h1>Original Display vs Duplicate Folder: Mobile Screen Badalne Se Pehle Yeh Zaroor Padhein</h1>
    <div class="meta-text">By 4 STAR MOBILE • 20+ Years Trusted Store • Kishanganj</div>

    <p>Mobile phone haath se chhoot kar girna aur screen ka toot jana bohot aam baat hai. Lekin jab hum display badalwane market mein nikalte hain, toh dukaandar puchte hain: <em>"Bhaiya, duplicate folder lagana hai ya original grade?"</em></p>
    
    <p>Aksar log kam daam ke chakkar mein aisi screen lagwa lete hain jo kuch hi dino mein pareshan karne lagti hai. Aaiye jaante hain dono mein kya bada farq hota hai:</p>

    <h2>1. Brightness Aur Dhup Mein Visibility</h2>
    <p>Original grade display (OLED/AMOLED ya high-quality IPS) mein natural colors aur high nits brightness hoti hai, jisse kadi dhoop mein bhi screen saaf dikhti hai. Duplicate local copy screens mein dhoop mein aate hi screen bilkul kaali dikhne lagti hai.</p>

    <h2>2. Touch Sensitivity Aur Typing Lag</h2>
    <p>Normal copy folder mein fast typing karte waqt akshar miss hote hain aur phone garam hone par 'Ghost Touch' (apne aap touch hona) ki samasya aati hai. Original quality screen mein 100% smooth scrolling milti hai.</p>

    <h2>3. Battery Consumption Aur Safety</h2>
    <div class="highlight-card">
      <strong>Khaas Baat:</strong> Sasti duplicate screen phone ki battery ko tezi se kheenchti hai kyunki uska display driver IC theek se optimize nahi hota, jisse mobile jaldi garam hota hai.
    </div>

    <h2>4. Frame Fitting Aur Edge Durability</h2>
    <p>Original folder phone ke frame mein bilkul barabar baithta hai, jisse kinaron se roshni (light leak) nahi jhaankti aur camera ya calling sensor theek se kaam karte hain.</p>

